because I have enjoyed those so much

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:19.323
as well as our times together
over breakfast, tea and lunch.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.500
Why am I here?

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:25.380
So sometime in, I think it was in 2018,

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:30.330
I had my first teaching relief
for, and I went on leave,

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:32.580
and I used that semester
so that was five years ago,

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.980
to really start pondering and reflecting,

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:37.140
I wanna know what I know, right?

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:38.790
Sometimes you feel like I only know

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.350
that I don't know anything,

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:41.820
but I wanted to know what I know.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:44.670
And I spent a lot of
time on that semester,

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:45.750
I put together a course

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.880
on scientific thinking and reasoning.

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:50.040
And one of the books that I went back to,

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.080
I knew this book, I don't
know how many of you know it,

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:53.617
it's from two British colleagues,

00:17:53.617 --> 00:17:55.300
"Stop Working &amp; Start Thinking."

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:58.170
And I think that cartoon says so much

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:01.110
of the challenge we face on a daily basis.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:05.610
We can seldom find time
to stop, ponder, reflect.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:07.320
I mean, just the pressures to get money,

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:09.420
we don't even know what
